From 3dcd69c35951cee4896458b6a8b68af9d70d6069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:24:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tokens,modal): add elevation/motion tokens and a
 DsModalComponent

Phase 1 gap-fill: the token pipeline covered color, typography, and
spacing but had no elevation (shadow) or motion (duration/easing)
scale, so every future overlay/transition would have hand-rolled its
own values. Adds tokens/elevation.tokens.json and
tokens/motion.tokens.json (DTCG format, matching the existing files),
wires them into style-dictionary.config.mjs and the generated-output
forwarding index, and adds a dark-mode scrim override.

Phase 2 gap-fill: Bootstrap's CSS is compiled in but its JS components
(modal, dropdown, tooltip, toast, etc.) were never wired up anywhere in
the library. Adds DsModalComponent as the first of that category, built
on the native <dialog> element (top-layer stacking, built-in focus trap
and focus restoration) rather than reimplementing that behavior, styled
with the new elevation/motion tokens. Includes unit tests, Storybook
stories, and an axe a11y e2e check, and wires it into the component
sandbox app and public API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
